01:21:45.860 --> 01:21:50.020
Um, the, uh, to to support
the resolution for a rental

01:21:50.020 --> 01:21:51.620
registry in Aurora.

01:21:52.180 --> 01:21:55.180
Um, as a community organizer
of canvas, numerous apartment

01:21:55.180 --> 01:21:58.540
complexes, particularly
in South Aurora.

01:21:58.700 --> 01:22:01.460
These are some of the stories
I heard from a huge apartment

01:22:01.460 --> 01:22:05.180
complex made up of dozens of
two storey buildings owned by a

01:22:05.180 --> 01:22:07.540
predatory corporate landlord.

01:22:07.580 --> 01:22:10.980
One resident said they had a
gas leak that wasn't fixed for

01:22:10.980 --> 01:22:11.990
three months.

01:22:12.150 --> 01:22:14.390
Another said they didn't
have a bedroom door.

01:22:14.430 --> 01:22:18.310
No locks on windows, no locks
on screen doors and didn't get

01:22:18.750 --> 01:22:20.990
anything fixed for eight months.

01:22:21.190 --> 01:22:25.430
One woman told me a story
where she had the boiler of the

01:22:25.430 --> 01:22:29.630
building in her closet, and
one, and started suffering from

01:22:29.630 --> 01:22:31.430
the impacts of black mold.

01:22:31.710 --> 01:22:35.030
She finally opened the closet
door and was able to put her

01:22:35.030 --> 01:22:38.150
finger through the wall
because of how damp it was.

01:22:39.310 --> 01:22:43.310
Um, this is these are just a
few of the many, many stories

01:22:43.310 --> 01:22:46.270
I've heard specifically
in South Aurora.

01:22:46.990 --> 01:22:50.190
And while there is an
inspection program that exists,

01:22:50.230 --> 01:22:53.950
unfortunately there are
landlords that have so much

01:22:53.950 --> 01:22:56.830
money that a slap on
the wrist is not enough.

01:22:56.870 --> 01:22:58.510
There needs to be real material

01:22:58.510 --> 01:23:00.550
consequences for
these landlords.

01:23:00.790 --> 01:23:04.190
If you're an irresponsible
driver, you lose your license.

01:23:04.190 --> 01:23:05.670
You lose the right to drive.

01:23:05.750 --> 01:23:08.430
If you don't do your
job, you don't get paid.

01:23:08.430 --> 01:23:09.670
You lose your job.

01:23:09.880 --> 01:23:12.400
If you're a bad landlord, you
shouldn't be able to collect

01:23:12.400 --> 01:23:15.160
rent and you actually shouldn't
be able to be a landlord.

01:23:16.760 --> 01:23:19.720
While critical legislation at
the state level has passed over

01:23:19.720 --> 01:23:23.120
the seven years, the last seven
years without enforcement and

01:23:23.120 --> 01:23:25.960
oversight, those laws
are just words on paper.

01:23:26.000 --> 01:23:28.920
It's up to local governments
to improve upon these laws.

01:23:28.960 --> 01:23:31.320
And one way to do this is
through a rental registry

01:23:31.320 --> 01:23:34.680
program to complement the
current inspection program.

01:23:35.280 --> 01:23:39.840
There's over 160 rental
registries currently that exist

01:23:39.840 --> 01:23:42.560
in the in the US, and while
most of them were initially

01:23:42.560 --> 01:23:46.560
created to be data driven,
the clear need here is to have

01:23:46.560 --> 01:23:49.080
oversight over predatory
landlords that threaten the

01:23:49.080 --> 01:23:50.720
stock of existing housing.

01:23:51.680 --> 01:23:53.920
There is a lack of data, but
more importantly, there is a

01:23:53.920 --> 01:23:55.160
public health issue in this

01:23:55.160 --> 01:23:57.240
city because of the
lack of oversight.

01:23:57.400 --> 01:24:00.960
If you care about housing,
health, affordability, youth,

01:24:00.960 --> 01:24:04.720
seniors, people with
disabilities and other impacted

01:24:04.760 --> 01:24:07.520
marginalized communities, you
will not only support this

01:24:07.640 --> 01:24:10.440
measure, but support the
creation of a rental registry

01:24:10.600 --> 01:24:13.280
through their leadership
of impacted communities.

01:24:13.320 --> 01:24:16.280
Regulating landlords actually
is an issue of life or death

01:24:16.280 --> 01:24:17.040
for some.

01:24:17.760 --> 01:24:22.080
Um, Aurora has a chance to
improve the lives of thousands

01:24:22.080 --> 01:24:24.280
of people, and that's
why we're here today.

