01:25:09.890 --> 01:25:13.970
Two sided research briefings
have been provided to all city

01:25:13.970 --> 01:25:16.450
Council members for your review.

01:25:16.770 --> 01:25:19.610
What we're asking for tonight
is grounded in what works.

01:25:20.210 --> 01:25:22.610
The council's decision to
advance a rental licensing

01:25:22.610 --> 01:25:25.450
process is the right move, and
I want to be direct about that

01:25:25.450 --> 01:25:28.010
word licensing what
it has to mean.

01:25:28.130 --> 01:25:30.010
A registry is just a list.

01:25:30.210 --> 01:25:32.970
It tells the city which
properties are rentals and

01:25:32.970 --> 01:25:33.810
that's it.

01:25:34.210 --> 01:25:37.170
A list cannot contact a
landlord when a tenant won't

01:25:37.170 --> 01:25:38.250
engage with the city.

01:25:38.490 --> 01:25:41.730
A list cannot build a
cross-departmental record that

01:25:41.730 --> 01:25:44.490
identifies and escalates
chronic violators.

01:25:44.930 --> 01:25:48.850
A list cannot protect tenants
moving into a unit that hasn't

01:25:48.850 --> 01:25:50.250
been inspected in years.

01:25:50.650 --> 01:25:52.730
Aurora's tenants and homeowners
need more than a list.

01:25:52.730 --> 01:25:56.810
They need a licensing program
for multifamily and rentals.

01:25:57.290 --> 01:26:01.170
A successful licensing program
for Aurora has three legs one

01:26:01.250 --> 01:26:05.460
access Aurora enhancement that
creates one persistent property

01:26:05.460 --> 01:26:07.380
record across departments.

01:26:07.540 --> 01:26:10.220
Automatically notifies the
landlord when a tenant won't

01:26:10.220 --> 01:26:14.940
engage, and flags repeat
violators for escalation to

01:26:15.180 --> 01:26:17.980
licensing and certificate of
occupancy requirements that

01:26:17.980 --> 01:26:20.660
ensure rental units meet
safety requirements.

01:26:20.780 --> 01:26:24.460
Safety minimums before
moving in three.

01:26:24.660 --> 01:26:27.860
A dedicated department like
boulders that provides the

01:26:27.860 --> 01:26:30.580
follow through that scattered
departments currently do not

01:26:30.580 --> 01:26:33.260
sustain alone as
a cautionary tale.

01:26:33.500 --> 01:26:35.380
Denver lost its program in 2020.

01:26:35.380 --> 01:26:38.940
Denver launched Excuse Me, its
program in 2021 without this

01:26:38.940 --> 01:26:40.020
type of infrastructure.

01:26:40.380 --> 01:26:41.980
Five years later, compliance

01:26:41.980 --> 01:26:44.700
sits at roughly 40% of
eligible properties.

01:26:44.740 --> 01:26:48.220
Chronic violators outlast the
fine structure, and this year,

01:26:48.260 --> 01:26:51.300
Denver is proposing to
retreat to a complaint based

01:26:51.300 --> 01:26:53.460
enforcement and cut
its staff entirely.

01:26:53.820 --> 01:26:57.020
They are retrofitting what they
didn't build in from the start.

01:26:57.060 --> 01:26:58.700
The licensing
wasn't the problem.

01:26:58.700 --> 01:27:00.380
The infrastructure was

01:27:01.390 --> 01:27:04.590
Aurora has the opportunity to
do this the right time, the

01:27:04.590 --> 01:27:05.830
right way the first time.

01:27:06.590 --> 01:27:09.510
Our ask is straightforward
design the ordinance and the

01:27:09.510 --> 01:27:11.030
infrastructure together.

01:27:11.150 --> 01:27:14.070
And when the working group
forms, make sure it includes

01:27:14.070 --> 01:27:18.310
