01:34:55.420 --> 01:34:58.580
My name is Janice, and I'm a
housing attorney at justice for

01:34:58.580 --> 01:34:59.820
the People Legal Center.

01:34:59.860 --> 01:35:02.660
I've been a housing attorney
in Colorado for four years,

01:35:02.660 --> 01:35:05.780
representing tenants throughout
the state, including in Aurora.

01:35:05.820 --> 01:35:09.740
And I'm here today to voice my
strong support of the rental

01:35:09.740 --> 01:35:11.780
registry and licensing program.

01:35:12.100 --> 01:35:15.740
This type of program is an
incredibly important tool in

01:35:15.740 --> 01:35:19.260
ensuring that the laws on the
books, laws that say that if a

01:35:19.260 --> 01:35:22.260
landlord chooses to rent
a unit, that unit must be

01:35:22.260 --> 01:35:25.700
livable, that those laws are
enforced, and that the renters

01:35:25.700 --> 01:35:30.060
in Aurora are living in safe
and habitable housing as it

01:35:30.060 --> 01:35:31.140
currently operates.

01:35:31.180 --> 01:35:34.260
The legal field alone is
not enough of an enforcement

01:35:34.260 --> 01:35:37.420
mechanism for warranty of
habitability violations.

01:35:38.020 --> 01:35:41.460
There are simply not enough
attorneys taking these cases.

01:35:41.500 --> 01:35:45.020
I work at a small nonprofit
law firm, one of the few

01:35:45.020 --> 01:35:47.260
organizations that
do take these cases.

01:35:47.260 --> 01:35:51.180
And we receive hundreds of
intakes from renters asking for

01:35:51.180 --> 01:35:53.780
help with severe
habitability violations.

01:35:54.380 --> 01:35:57.020
With our limited capacity,
we can only assist a small

01:35:57.020 --> 01:36:00.500
fraction of these renters,
leaving a huge number of

01:36:00.500 --> 01:36:04.100
renters in Aurora and across
the state with legitimate

01:36:04.100 --> 01:36:06.340
claims and without
legal representation.

01:36:07.740 --> 01:36:10.900
Even when we can assist and
when we can pursue class action

01:36:10.900 --> 01:36:14.420
litigation to help all
similarly situated tenants, the

01:36:14.420 --> 01:36:19.260
relief that these renters can
receive takes years, which

01:36:19.300 --> 01:36:20.820
often translates as tenants.

01:36:20.820 --> 01:36:24.740
In the meantime, living either
in substandard conditions or

01:36:24.740 --> 01:36:25.820
being displaced.

01:36:26.220 --> 01:36:30.140
And these are the tenants who
are willing and able to fight

01:36:30.140 --> 01:36:31.660
to enforce their rights.

01:36:32.020 --> 01:36:35.020
Previously, when I was an
eviction defense attorney, I

01:36:35.020 --> 01:36:39.060
saw too many tenants, including
Aurora residents, facing

01:36:39.140 --> 01:36:42.910
horrible living conditions but
falling through the cracks from

01:36:42.910 --> 01:36:45.990
a single mother who had no
heat, so she and all of her

01:36:45.990 --> 01:36:47.310
children had to sleep together

01:36:47.310 --> 01:36:49.070
in the living room to stay warm.

01:36:49.070 --> 01:36:52.950
But because she rightfully
feared retaliation, she was

01:36:52.950 --> 01:36:56.630
unwilling to pursue the legal
recourse available to her to a

01:36:56.630 --> 01:36:59.870
family that was already evicted
that could not get the evidence

01:36:59.870 --> 01:37:03.150
necessary to show rampant,
unmitigated mold was causing

01:37:03.150 --> 01:37:05.790
severe respiratory and skin
infections in themselves and

01:37:05.790 --> 01:37:06.670
their children.

01:37:07.230 --> 01:37:09.830
The rental registry and
licensing program that would

01:37:09.830 --> 01:37:12.550
require compliance with
code enforcement in order to

01:37:12.590 --> 01:37:15.830
maintain licensure, would
create accountability for

01:37:15.830 --> 01:37:20.390
landlords and prevent aurora
renters from living in

01:37:20.390 --> 01:37:23.430
unlivable and
illegal conditions.

01:37:25.030 --> 01:37:27.150
I ask that you support
this resolution.

01:37:27.230 --> 01:37:28.190
Thank you.

