list of what was
already up for priority.

02:23:53.950 --> 02:23:57.110
So you essentially gave the
community a list that you've

02:23:57.110 --> 02:24:01.710
already decided was necessary,
and then ask them to affirm or

02:24:01.710 --> 02:24:04.480
buy in to the list that
you've already curated.

02:24:05.600 --> 02:24:08.960
Who was in the room that
actually gave you a raw,

02:24:08.960 --> 02:24:13.280
intentional, lived experience
of what transportation should

02:24:13.280 --> 02:24:14.040
look like?

02:24:14.200 --> 02:24:16.600
Public safety and
community facilities.

02:24:17.640 --> 02:24:18.440
Instead,

02:24:19.560 --> 02:24:24.280
there were 54 meetings of
engagement that had already

02:24:24.280 --> 02:24:27.360
preconditioned what this
is supposed to look like.

02:24:29.080 --> 02:24:31.440
So I am imploring you all

02:24:32.480 --> 02:24:37.360
to push pause and to not push
this through until you actually

02:24:37.400 --> 02:24:39.800
formally do the work of what it

02:24:39.800 --> 02:24:42.560
means to engage
community thoughtfully.

02:24:44.000 --> 02:24:47.680
And oftentimes, I will hear
leaders say, I don't know how

02:24:47.680 --> 02:24:49.000
to engage the community.

02:24:49.040 --> 02:24:50.960
How do I get them to show up?

02:24:52.280 --> 02:24:56.000
You don't get them to show up
by by making something happen

02:24:56.000 --> 02:24:56.760
to them.

02:24:57.720 --> 02:25:00.560
You have them show up when
something is going to happen

02:25:00.560 --> 02:25:01.520
with them.

02:25:03.450 --> 02:25:07.410
The city has never birthed
trust with its constituency.

02:25:09.010 --> 02:25:12.730
And now you're asking your
constituents to finance

02:25:12.730 --> 02:25:16.010
something on layers of trust.

02:25:16.650 --> 02:25:18.570
Trust that you have not earned.

02:25:18.930 --> 02:25:21.210
I recommend you postpone this.

02:25:23.050 --> 02:25:24.490
Agent Anderson.

02:25:32.730 --> 02:25:37.330
Mayor and members of City
council who actually show up to

02:25:37.370 --> 02:25:38.410
work today.

02:25:38.810 --> 02:25:44.250
Aurora absolutely deserves to
have safer streets, stronger

02:25:44.250 --> 02:25:47.730
bridges, better intersections,
and transportation

02:25:47.770 --> 02:25:49.290
infrastructure that serves

02:25:49.290 --> 02:25:51.330
every one of Aurora's
neighborhoods.

02:25:51.570 --> 02:25:55.970
But supporting transportation
investment does not require us

02:25:55.970 --> 02:25:59.930
to support this
proposal as written.

02:26:00.500 --> 02:26:02.740
This measure asks residents to

02:26:02.740 --> 02:26:06.740
approve a new sales
tax for 31 years.

02:26:07.060 --> 02:26:12.020
Authorize up to $108 million
in debt, and accept a maximum

02:26:12.020 --> 02:26:15.140
repayment cost of
nearly $210 million.

02:26:15.340 --> 02:26:17.500
That is not a small request.

02:26:17.620 --> 02:26:22.180
That is a generational
long financial commitment.

02:26:22.620 --> 02:26:25.660
And yet, the language before
you today does not provide

02:26:25.660 --> 02:26:28.140
residents with a
binding project.

02:26:28.140 --> 02:26:32.100
List a clear construction
timeline, or guarantee that the

02:26:32.100 --> 02:26:33.340
neighborhoods with the greatest

02:26:33.340 --> 02:26:35.660
transportation needs
will be prioritized.

02:26:36.500 --> 02:26:41.180
The phrase including but not
limited to, gives the city

02:26:41.180 --> 02:26:45.580
broad discretion to decide
how this money will be spent.

02:26:45.940 --> 02:26:49.700
Voters are being asked to
approve the new tax and trust

02:26:49.700 --> 02:26:51.780
that the details
will come afterwards.

02:26:51.940 --> 02:26:54.100
That is simply not enough.

02:26:54.460 --> 02:26:56.260
A sales tax is also one of the

02:26:56.260 --> 02:26:58.630
most regressive ways
to raise revenue.

02:26:58.670 --> 02:27:02.550
It asks working families,
renters, seniors and low income

02:27:02.550 --> 02:27:06.150
residents to pay a larger share
of their income every time they

02:27:06.150 --> 02:27:07.950
make a taxable purchase.

02:27:08.150 --> 02:27:11.430
Before asking those families
for more money, the city should

02:27:11.430 --> 02:27:15.350
be able to show them exactly
what they are paying for.

02:27:16.070 --> 02:27:18.630
When will it be built and how

02:27:18.630 --> 02:27:20.310
their neighborhood will benefit?

02:27:20.310 --> 02:27:23.710
And the public deserves a
direct answer to another

02:27:23.710 --> 02:27:24.870
important question.

02:27:24.870 --> 02:27:28.950
If one of the the ballot
measures does not pass and

02:27:28.950 --> 02:27:31.390
another one does pass.

02:27:31.430 --> 02:27:35.630
Will the city attempt to shift
or supplement redirect any

02:27:35.630 --> 02:27:38.510
available funds to advance
projects that voters

02:27:38.510 --> 02:27:43.030
specifically rejected because a
failed ballot measure must mean

02:27:43.030 --> 02:27:46.870
something the city should not
be allowed to use accounting

02:27:46.870 --> 02:27:51.150
maneuvers, budget transfers,
or other funding mechanisms to

02:27:51.150 --> 02:27:54.870
accomplish indirectly
what voters have rejected.

02:27:55.190 --> 02:28:00.070
If the public says no to a
particular tax or project, that

02:28:00.070 --> 02:28:02.270
decision must be respected.

02:28:02.510 --> 02:28:07.390
I joined Madiun and other
organizations and ask you to

02:28:07.430 --> 02:28:09.670
